WEBVTT

00:03:27.911 --> 00:03:30.832
Despite being a stone's throw
from the Kremlin,

00:03:30.856 --> 00:03:33.696
we decided to focus
on Moscow's aspirations

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.966
of becoming a progressive,
cosmopolitan city.

00:03:37.553 --> 00:03:39.871
As national governments are failing us,

00:03:39.895 --> 00:03:42.628
cities hold the promise of social reform.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.057
The park would be a site
of civic expression,

00:03:46.081 --> 00:03:47.978
a foil to the military parades

00:03:48.002 --> 00:03:50.985
and other demonstrations
of power in Red Square.

00:03:51.985 --> 00:03:54.644
Given the vulnerability
that public spaces pose

00:03:54.668 --> 00:03:55.839
from opposition,

00:03:55.863 --> 00:03:57.996
governments try to control them.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.696
The architectural brief we got
discouraged large open spaces,